            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "PetitCreamPuff"
            },
            "reviewBody": "YUM!!!!!!! So fluffy and creamy. Tastes very \"refreshing\" because of the zucchini. Definitely a keeper"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "terze"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Will make again. Was definitely sweet, I’ll cut back 1/2 cup at least next time. I added 1/4 cup lemon juice and skipped the cinnamon sugar on top, was good, but I couldn’t taste the lemon, i was thinking so they would be more like a lemon bar, next time I’ll add more juice and some zest and maybe a drop or two of lemon oil. It is way to thick, next time I’ll double the crust and put in a cookie sheet and make only one recipe of filling. It was like a pumpkin pie, same ingredients, squash, eggs, sugar, and canned milk, i was thinking more like a creamy pudding custard type thing but it’s just like a pie. I can’t wait to try it again with my modifications and also to make it a day ahead to set. Oh ya cook at least 20 more minuets linger,",
            "datePublished": "2018-06-22T15:32:56.143Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Linda T"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I was really concerned when I poured the zucchini puree on top of the crust. It was almost as thin as water. I put it in the oven, carefully and it firmed up quite a bit. A couple of changes I think I'd make to the recipe next time - a little more flour in the filling. For me, the filling is still a bit too loose. I'd also reduce the sugar as it seems very sweet to me, The crust was delicious as it was,, Update - I stuck these back in the oven and baked them some more.. maybe another 30 minutes. The sugar turned more caramalized and the bars firmed up and browned. I like them MUCH better this way! So if you make these and don't like them, bake them more and you might be surprised",
            "datePublished": "2012-01-14T19:32:46.573Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Samantha Zielke"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great recipe. I also cooked this for about 20-30 mins more than the original recipe calls for, bars firmed up better. I also didn't have 2 tsp of Vanilla Extract (oops) so I used just 1 tsp and it tastes great. Great way to get rid of these zucchini! :)",
            "datePublished": "2014-07-27T06:13:38.210Z"
          },
          {
